From l.karssen at erasmusmc.nl  Wed Dec  7 11:03:52 2011
From: l.karssen at erasmusmc.nl (L.C. Karssen)
Date: Wed, 07 Dec 2011 11:03:52 +0100
Subject: [GenABEL-dev] export.plink() uses too much memory in GenABEL v1.7-0
	(beta)
Message-ID: <4EDF3A08.4050409@erasmusmc.nl>

Dear list,

We just tried to convert a GenABEL object to plink format using 
export.plink() from GenABEL v 1.7-0 (still under development, package 
built from SVN yesterday), and it nearly brought the machine to a halt 
because it used all available memory (RAM + swap).

Our GenABEL object contained almost 3700 individuals and about 700k SNPS.

Have others experienced this as well? I haven't looked at Yurii's latest 
implementation of the function in C++ yet. Hopefully I will be able to 
find some time later today. Does anyone here know how we could limit 
memory usage in C++?


Thanks,

Lennart.

